How to Fix the Error
You have two main options to resolve this:

Option 1: Compile as a 32-bit program (Recommended for this code)
If you want to keep the code as 32-bit assembly, you must explicitly instruct your assembler and linker to target 32-bit architecture.

Run the following commands in your terminal:

# Assemble with the 32-bit flag
as --32 test.S -o test.o

# Link with the 32-bit ELF emulation flag
ld -m elf_i386 test.o -o test

Option 2: Rewrite the code for 64-bit x86_64
If you are running a modern 64-bit system, it is usually better to write native 64-bit assembly. 
This requires changing pushl to pushq, using 64-bit registers (%rbp, %rsp), 
and updating the calling convention.

